ja:
確定運動量$p_0$を持つ状態は固有値方程式を満たす。 $\hat p_x\psi_{p_0}(x)=p_0\psi_{p_0}(x).$ $\hat p_x$の微分形式を代入すると $-i\hbar\frac{d\psi_{p_0}(x)}{dx}
=p_0\psi_{p_0}(x).$ 波動関数の導関数は波動関数自体に比例するので、解は指数関数の形をとる。 $\psi_{p_0}(x)\propto
\exp\left(\frac{ip_0x}{\hbar}\right).$

zh:
一个具有确定动量$p_0$的态满足本征值方程 $\hat p_x\psi_{p_0}(x)=p_0\psi_{p_0}(x).$ 代入$\hat p_x$的微分形式给出 $-i\hbar\frac{d\psi_{p_0}(x)}{dx}
=p_0\psi_{p_0}(x).$ 波函数的导数与波函数本身成正比，所以解具有指数形式： $\psi_{p_0}(x)\propto
\exp\left(\frac{ip_0x}{\hbar}\right).$

p.src:
Now evolve a state from $t$ to $t+\epsilon$: $\begin{aligned}\ket{\psi(t+\epsilon)}
&=
U(\epsilon)\ket{\psi(t)}
\\
&=
\left(
\mathbf 1-\frac{i\epsilon}{\hbar}H
\right)\ket{\psi(t)}
+\mathcal O(\epsilon^2).\end{aligned}$ Subtracting $\ket{\psi(t)}$, dividing by $\epsilon$, and taking the limit gives $\frac{d}{dt}\ket{\psi(t)}
=
-\frac{i}{\hbar}H\ket{\psi(t)}.$ Equivalently, $i\hbar\frac{d}{dt}\ket{\psi(t)}
=
H\ket{\psi(t)}.$ This is the time-dependent Schrödinger equation. In the position representation it becomes $i\hbar\frac{\partial}{\partial t}\psi(x,t)
=
H\psi(x,t),$ where $H$ acts as an operator on the wavefunction.

